Package: tpattern
Title: Open, Auditable T-Pattern Analysis (R Interface to the 'tpattern' Python Library)
Version: 0.1.15
Authors@R:
    person("Andy", "Callaway", email = "acallaway@bournemouth.ac.uk", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Detects recurring temporal patterns (T-patterns; Magnusson, 2000
    <doi:10.3758/BF03200792>) in sequences of timed, labelled events and tests
    them against chance with correction for repeated testing. This package is a
    thin, idiomatic R interface to the 'tpattern' Python library, called through
    'reticulate'. The detection algorithm and statistics live in Python, so
    results match the Python package, the Colab notebooks and the published
    paper exactly; there is a single source of truth. A data-driven advisor
    inspects your data and recommends the analysis settings (which surrogate
    null, whether to require a genuine lag, which error control), with reasons,
    and you decide whether to follow it.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
Encoding: UTF-8
Language: en-GB
Imports:
    reticulate (>= 1.30)
Suggests:
    testthat (>= 3.0.0)
SystemRequirements: Python (>= 3.9) with the 'tpattern' package; install it once
    from R with install_tpattern().
